{"tail":"\n          "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n12.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"When a festival is immediately followed by the Sabbath, food intended for the Sabbath may be prepared on a day of the festival only if bread and some cooked or roasted food (a piece of meat or fish) have been prepared and set aside for the Sabbath on the eve of the festival. The master of the house takes the bread and cooked food in his hand and recites the following in the presence of the housewife:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n          "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:eruv_tavshilin@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-heidenheim-1965-he"}}
